The Arctic Tern's unique identifying traits include its striking coloration, particularly the contrast between the black cap and white underparts, as well as its long, pointed wings and forked tail. These features help distinguish it from other tern species, such as the Common Tern, which has a more rounded tail and lacks the black cap. Additionally, the Arctic Tern's red bill and legs are distinctive and can be used to identify the species.
