Behaviorally, Fish Crows are highly intelligent and adaptable, often found near water bodies where they feed on fish, crustaceans, and other aquatic creatures. They are known for their curiosity and problem-solving abilities, as well as their ability to mimic human speech and sounds. Their calls are loud and varied, often described as a "caw" or "kaw."

In terms of unique identifying traits, Fish Crows can be distinguished by their relatively large size compared to other crows, their distinct call, and their preference for coastal habitats.
